king: 抽一次烟). Chinese does not mark part of speech, so this is not a part-of-speech error.\n- A usage note in brackets such as （表示…）, alongside an equivalent or in place of one.\nfail when any of these holds:\n- It means something else, or any listed equivalent is wrong for this sense, even when a bracketed note explains the usage correctly.\n- For a verb sense, an equivalent only names a thing or quality and cannot be used as a verb.\n- It renders a phrase or phrasal verb that contains the word instead of the word in this sense.\n- It renders a different sense of the word, such as one of the other senses listed below.\n- It is unnatural or ungrammatical in the target language.\n- It lists equivalents of several unrelated senses.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (noun) \"One of the parts of a bird, bat, or insect used for flying.\"\n- (noun) \"A section of a building that extends from the main part.\"\n- (noun) \"A group within a political party or organization with particular views or responsibilities.\"\n- (noun) \"One of the areas at the sides of a theatre stage hidden from the audience.\"\n- (noun) \"Either side of the playing field in certain team sports.\"\n- (noun) \"A player who plays near the side of the field in certain team sports.\"\n- (noun) \"A body panel covering a wheel of a motor vehicle.\"\n- (noun) \"A bird''s wing prepared or served as food.\"\n- (noun) \"A military aviation unit consisting of several squadrons.\"\n- (verb) \"To fly or travel swiftly through the air.\"\n- (verb) \"To perform or deal with something without preparation.\"\n- (verb) \"To wound a bird in a wing or a person in an arm with a shot.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"wing","pos":"noun","gloss":"One of the flat structures extending from the sides of an aircraft that provide lift.","siblings":[{"pos":"noun","gloss":"One of the parts of a bird, bat, or insect used for flying."},{"pos":"noun","gloss":"A section of a building that extends from the main part."},{