ble) unless the vowel before it is short and stressed, which keeps it (fam·i·ly, stud·y, cas·u·al); a doubled consonant splits (lit·tle, dif·fer·ent); inside a group of consonants any break a natural pronunciation allows will do. Word parts and a dictionary''s print hyphenation do not decide a break: com·fort·a·ble and en·able are wrong here, since the word''s parts are recorded in its morphology.\nA one-syllable word is one part.\npass: each part is one vowel sound of the careful pronunciation, with its breaks where the rule puts them.\nfail: a part holds two vowel sounds or none, a vowel sound of the careful pronunciation is joined to its neighbour, or a break follows word parts or print hyphenation against the pronunciation.\nSenses recorded for it so far:\n- (noun) \"A living being, especially an animal.\"\n- (noun) \"An imaginary or strange being.\"\n- (noun) \"A person or animal regarded with affection, pity, or contempt.\"\n- (noun) \"A person or organization controlled by or dependent on another person or organization.\""}}}]},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"creature","senses":[{"id":"b27a4c22-8ffb-4be7-8f4f-3dc845cd49b3","pos":"noun","gloss":"A living being, especially an animal."},{"id":"84963dd5-f563-43d1-8751-ceb3c0d89dc7","pos":"noun","gloss":"An imaginary or strange being."},{"id":"4bcbf854-e6cc-4609-93c2-0a62fe723bf7","pos":"noun","gloss":"A person or animal regarded with affection, pity, or contempt."},{"id":"1fc97e5f-0126-454e-a0b5-89b77259e7d5","pos":"noun","gloss":"A person or organization controlled by or dependent on another person or organization."}],"caseVariants":[]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-12T17:27:17.801Z"}', '2026-11-10T19:52:28.450Z', '2026-11-12T17:27:17.801Z', '', NULL);
