Chinese does not mark part of speech, so this is not a part-of-speech error.\n- A usage note in brackets such as （表示…）, alongside an equivalent or in place of one.\nfail when any of these holds:\n- It means something else, or any listed equivalent is wrong for this sense, even when a bracketed note explains the usage correctly.\n- For a verb sense, an equivalent only names a thing or quality and cannot be used as a verb.\n- It renders a phrase or phrasal verb that contains the word instead of the word in this sense.\n- It renders a different sense of the word, such as one of the other senses listed below.\n- It is unnatural or ungrammatical in the target language.\n- It lists equivalents of several unrelated senses.\nOther senses of this entry, for reference:\n- (adjective) \"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable.\"\n- (adjective) \"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game.\"\n- (adjective) \"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand.\"\n- (adjective) \"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest.\"\n- (adjective) \"Sexually attractive.\"\n- (adjective) \"Feeling strong sexual desire.\"\n- (adjective) \"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very skilful at a particular activity or knowledgeable about a particular subject.\"\n- (adjective) \"Newly obtained or produced and very recent.\"\n- (adjective) \"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very interested in or eager for something.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very likely to win or succeed.\"\n- (adjective) \"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed.\"\n- (adjective) \"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock.\"\n- (adjective) \"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble.\"\n- (adjective) \"Very bright and strong in colour.\""}},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"hot","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Containing sexual material that is intended to excite people.","siblings":[{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a high temperature or a temperature higher than is comfortable."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Recent enough to provide promising clues about someone or something being sought."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very close to finding a hidden object or guessing the correct answer in a game."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Having a strong taste that causes a burning feeling in the mouth."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very popular, fashionable, or in great demand."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Causing strong disagreement, excitement, or public interest."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Sexually attractive."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Feeling strong sexual desire."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Stolen and therefore risky to possess or sell."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very skilful at a particular activity or knowledgeable about a particular subject."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Newly obtained or produced and very recent."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Involving intense activity, competition, or emotion."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very interested in or eager for something."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very likely to win or succeed."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Strict or insistent about making sure a rule or standard is followed."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Carrying an electric current that could cause an electric shock."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Dangerous or likely to cause trouble."},{"pos":"adjective","gloss":"Very bright and strong in colour."}]},"target":null,"topic":null,"attempts":[]},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-10T18:28:30.727Z"}', '2026-11-10T18:27:59.228Z', '2026-11-10T18:28:30.727Z', 'zh', NULL);
