less the vowel before it is short and stressed, which keeps it (fam·i·ly, stud·y, cas·u·al); a doubled consonant splits (lit·tle, dif·fer·ent); inside a group of consonants any break a natural pronunciation allows will do. Word parts and a dictionary''s print hyphenation do not decide a break: com·fort·a·ble and en·able are wrong here, since the word''s parts are recorded in its morphology.\nA one-syllable word is one part.\npass: each part is one vowel sound of the careful pronunciation, with its breaks where the rule puts them.\nfail: a part holds two vowel sounds or none, a vowel sound of the careful pronunciation is joined to its neighbour, or a break follows word parts or print hyphenation against the pronunciation.\nSenses recorded for it so far:\n- (noun) \"A living creature that is not a plant or a human, such as a dog, bird, fish or insect.\"\n- (noun) \"Any living creature, including a human, as opposed to a plant.\"\n- (adjective) \"Relating to animals or derived from animals.\"\n- (noun) \"A person who behaves in a cruel, violent, or uncivilized way.\"\n- (noun) \"A person or thing of a particular type.\"\n- (adjective) \"Relating to physical appetites and instincts rather than reason or spiritual qualities.\""}}}]},"context":{"subject":{"lemma":"animal","senses":[{"id":"f816f9b8-4a89-4b2a-9cb2-424ff9c72a3f","pos":"noun","gloss":"A living creature that is not a plant or a human, such as a dog, bird, fish or insect."},{"id":"cbcbbe15-4e8b-4732-8707-49ace61b3c23","pos":"noun","gloss":"Any living creature, including a human, as opposed to a plant."},{"id":"ee2f1833-230d-4427-a60d-5e693f40e930","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Relating to animals or derived from animals."},{"id":"715cf83d-8d69-4f47-9251-5b81317e69f7","pos":"noun","gloss":"A person who behaves in a cruel, violent, or uncivilized way."},{"id":"9f7d682a-d218-4bd4-961c-9689d44c22b3","pos":"noun","gloss":"A person or thing of a particular type."},{"id":"bdf88512-73ef-42f4-8639-bffa1020f37d","pos":"adjective","gloss":"Relating to physical appetites and instincts rather than reason or spiritual qualities."}],"caseVariants":[]},"target":null,"topic":null},"reviewed_at":"2026-11-12T17:18:34.091Z"}', '2026-11-10T07:29:36.950Z', '2026-11-12T17:18:34.091Z', '', NULL);
